<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<qti-assessment-item xmlns="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/imsqtiasi_v3p0" identifier="inlineChoice-reference" title="inlineChoice-reference" time-dependent="false" xml:lang="en">
  <qti-response-declaration identifier="RESPONSE_DECLARATION" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier">
    <qti-correct-response><qti-value>A</qti-value></qti-correct-response>
  </qti-response-declaration>
  <qti-response-declaration identifier="RESPONSE_OUTCOME" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier">
    <qti-correct-response><qti-value>B</qti-value></qti-correct-response>
  </qti-response-declaration>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="SCORE" cardinality="single" base-type="float">
    <qti-default-value><qti-value>0</qti-value></qti-default-value>
  </qti-outcome-declaration>
  <qti-item-body>
    <p>Reference item for inlineChoice-reference: QTI 3.0 item-player conformance fixture.</p>
    <p>In QTI 3.0, an interaction writes a candidate answer to a <qti-inline-choice-interaction response-identifier="RESPONSE_DECLARATION"><qti-inline-choice identifier="A">response declaration</qti-inline-choice><qti-inline-choice identifier="B">template declaration</qti-inline-choice><qti-inline-choice identifier="C">rubric block</qti-inline-choice></qti-inline-choice-interaction>, and response processing writes derived values such as SCORE to an <qti-inline-choice-interaction response-identifier="RESPONSE_OUTCOME"><qti-inline-choice identifier="A">item body</qti-inline-choice><qti-inline-choice identifier="B">outcome declaration</qti-inline-choice><qti-inline-choice identifier="C">choice interaction</qti-inline-choice></qti-inline-choice-interaction>.</p>
  </qti-item-body>
  <qti-response-processing template="https://purl.imsglobal.org/spec/qti/v3p0/rptemplates/match_correct"/>
</qti-assessment-item>
